      "writtenOn": "2022-12-09T20:27:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think your suggestion is the correct approach. Using naming convention is brittle and might result in errors in the future that are hard to detect.\n\nI just looked at `droidstubs` definition in go/Android.bp, and such a property exists today (`api_levels_sdk_type`). We can probably populate this property for java_sdk_library and the relelvant droidstubs module in `frameworks/base/StubLibraries.bp`\n\nI will look into creating this in a followup CL. jihoonkang@ is also working on checking in java_api_contribution soong modules into the tree for single_tree builds. When they are available, perhaps api_bp2build converters can plug into them directly and drop this naming convention use altogether.",
      "parentUuid": "67d13b93_596726a0",
